1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,211
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

2
00:00:03,294 --> 00:00:08,466
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

3
00:00:08,550 --> 00:00:10,593
- <i>♪ Fix this</i> ♪
- <i>♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

4
00:00:10,677 --> 00:00:12,762
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

5
00:00:12,846 --> 00:00:16,641
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

6
00:00:16,725 --> 00:00:17,976
[Atoy] <i>You were just together earlier.</i>

7
00:00:18,059 --> 00:00:19,352
<i>Where's Ibyang?</i>

8
00:00:19,436 --> 00:00:20,395
[Janine stammers]

9
00:00:20,478 --> 00:00:23,148
What are you doing here?
You're too young to be wandering around.

10
00:00:23,231 --> 00:00:25,400
I was with Tatoy and Janine.

11
00:00:25,483 --> 00:00:28,611
We were going to watch a movie,
but I got left behind.

12
00:00:28,695 --> 00:00:29,529
[Tonet] Atoy!

13
00:00:30,405 --> 00:00:32,407
- Where are you going?
- Did you follow me?

14
00:00:32,490 --> 00:00:34,117
‪PREVIOUSLY

15
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:35,160
So, come with me.

16
00:00:35,243 --> 00:00:36,327
[Emerson] There!

17
00:00:36,411 --> 00:00:37,829
[Emerson] At last!

18
00:00:37,912 --> 00:00:41,291
I'll go ahead because Tonet and I
have a lechon date.

19
00:00:41,374 --> 00:00:42,292
- [Emerson] Oh, Atoy-- Ouch.
- [teenager] Hey!

20
00:00:43,084 --> 00:00:44,252
Ouch. Hey!

21
00:00:44,335 --> 00:00:45,628
- [guard] <i>Come on, come on!</i>
- [Red] Uh… We're…

22
00:00:45,712 --> 00:00:46,671
- [Tonet shrieks]
- [groans]

23
00:00:50,800 --> 00:00:52,927
[Atoy] You really made me run after you.
Give me my friend's wallet.

24
00:00:53,011 --> 00:00:54,304
[teenager] Wallet, wallet.

25
00:00:54,387 --> 00:00:55,597
Oh, keep it!

26
00:00:55,680 --> 00:00:57,265
I need the voucher. It's important to him.

27
00:00:57,348 --> 00:00:58,391
- Give me the voucher.
- Take it.

28
00:00:58,475 --> 00:01:01,269
[dramatic stinging]

29
00:01:01,352 --> 00:01:02,979
Give me your wallet first.

30
00:01:03,063 --> 00:01:04,355
[grunts and groans]

31
00:01:04,439 --> 00:01:05,899
- [thumps]
- [weapons swoosh]

32
00:01:05,982 --> 00:01:06,900
[grunts]

33
00:01:06,983 --> 00:01:08,193
[Tonet] <i>Good thing I escaped from there.</i>

34
00:01:08,276 --> 00:01:09,235
[Martina, in English]
That's what you think.

35
00:01:09,319 --> 00:01:10,153
‪[dramatic stinging]

36
00:01:14,199 --> 00:01:15,033
[music fades]

37
00:01:15,116 --> 00:01:16,326
[grunting and groaning]

38
00:01:16,409 --> 00:01:19,037
[thumps, clangs, and swooshes]

39
00:01:19,120 --> 00:01:21,956
- [rock music playing]
- [grunting]

40
00:01:25,710 --> 00:01:27,337
- [swooshing]
- [thumps]

41
00:01:27,420 --> 00:01:28,338
[groans]

42
00:01:34,302 --> 00:01:35,845
Girl, that's enough!

43
00:01:35,929 --> 00:01:37,722
- [thumps]
- [groans]

44
00:01:38,431 --> 00:01:39,682
- [grunts]
- [thumps]

45
00:01:39,766 --> 00:01:41,935
[suave theme music playing]

46
00:01:42,018 --> 00:01:43,853
[motorcycle revving]

47
00:01:43,937 --> 00:01:44,813
[sewing machine whirring]

48
00:01:44,896 --> 00:01:45,772
[scratches]

49
00:01:45,855 --> 00:01:47,106
[snipping]

50
00:01:48,399 --> 00:01:51,653
[sewing machine clacking]

51
00:01:51,736 --> 00:01:53,696
- [gun cocks]
- [gunshots]

52
00:01:53,780 --> 00:01:55,031
[thumps and gunshots]

53
00:01:55,115 --> 00:01:57,325
[clicking]

54
00:01:57,408 --> 00:01:59,410
- [clicking]
- [snipping]

55
00:02:01,079 --> 00:02:02,413
[electronic blipping]

56
00:02:05,500 --> 00:02:06,584
[music fades]

57
00:02:06,668 --> 00:02:08,086
Can you stop?!

58
00:02:08,670 --> 00:02:11,381
Leave me alone!
I already have a quiet life!

59
00:02:11,464 --> 00:02:13,550
- [ominous music playing]
- [gasping]

60
00:02:13,633 --> 00:02:16,553
Our lives were quiet too,
then you suddenly came.

61
00:02:17,053 --> 00:02:19,055
Showing off with your suspicions.

62
00:02:19,139 --> 00:02:21,099
[in English] And now, here you are.

63
00:02:21,182 --> 00:02:23,601
Running, hiding,

64
00:02:24,185 --> 00:02:26,813
because you became a meddler!

65
00:02:26,896 --> 00:02:29,941
So, whose fault is that really?

66
00:02:30,024 --> 00:02:32,652
I just wanted to correct what Atoy knows!

67
00:02:32,735 --> 00:02:36,322
Don't you feel guilty that they're
recognizing the wrong child?!

68
00:02:36,406 --> 00:02:38,449
You're toying with them!

69
00:02:40,743 --> 00:02:42,954
[in English] That's no longer
your problem, Tonet.

70
00:02:43,538 --> 00:02:45,790
[clangs]

71
00:02:47,876 --> 00:02:50,295
- [grunting]
- [tense music playing]

72
00:02:51,170 --> 00:02:52,297
[Mongki whoops]

73
00:02:52,380 --> 00:02:54,173
[Mongki cackles]

74
00:02:54,257 --> 00:02:56,050
[Mongki] At last, I can get back
at you now!

75
00:02:56,134 --> 00:02:57,719
- [Mongki smirks]
- [music fades]

76
00:02:58,928 --> 00:03:00,638
- [swooshing]
- [rock music playing]

77
00:03:00,722 --> 00:03:03,850
[thumps, thuds]

78
00:03:05,059 --> 00:03:06,269
[groans]

79
00:03:07,604 --> 00:03:08,813
Ouch!

80
00:03:08,897 --> 00:03:09,731
- [music swells]
- [grunts]

81
00:03:09,814 --> 00:03:11,691
[whistle blowing]

82
00:03:11,774 --> 00:03:13,067
Hey, stop!

83
00:03:13,151 --> 00:03:15,987
- [music continues]
- [clamoring]

84
00:03:16,070 --> 00:03:17,488
You go there, I go here!

85
00:03:18,072 --> 00:03:20,491
- [Tonet shrieks]
- [tense music playing]

86
00:03:20,575 --> 00:03:22,327
[grunting and groaning]

87
00:03:22,410 --> 00:03:25,747
- [shouts]
- [shrieks]

88
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:30,793
[Martina, in English] You're so annoying!

89
00:03:30,877 --> 00:03:35,340
[grunting, gasping]

90
00:03:39,844 --> 00:03:41,888
[grunts]

91
00:03:42,513 --> 00:03:43,723
[grunting]

92
00:03:43,806 --> 00:03:46,017
[grunting and groaning]

93
00:03:46,100 --> 00:03:48,978
[grunting]

94
00:03:49,062 --> 00:03:50,355
[Tonet shouts]

95
00:03:51,981 --> 00:03:55,693
[grunts, groaning]

96
00:03:55,777 --> 00:03:56,694
[shouts]

97
00:03:56,778 --> 00:03:57,612
‪[groaning]

98
00:04:03,326 --> 00:04:06,454
[clanging and clattering]

99
00:04:09,707 --> 00:04:10,792
[clangs]

100
00:04:10,875 --> 00:04:11,918
[swishes]

101
00:04:12,585 --> 00:04:13,628
[music fades]

102
00:04:13,711 --> 00:04:19,008
[muffled chattering]

103
00:04:19,592 --> 00:04:21,344
- Oh.
- Looks like it hit-- There!

104
00:04:21,427 --> 00:04:24,222
Because of this voucher, many got hurt.

105
00:04:24,806 --> 00:04:27,308
But at least, you can still get
a discount on your…

106
00:04:27,392 --> 00:04:29,269
lechon date with Tonet.

107
00:04:29,352 --> 00:04:31,187
Thank you. Thank you, bro! Thank you, bro.

108
00:04:31,271 --> 00:04:33,231
Wait, the voucher's here,
but where's my wallet?

109
00:04:33,314 --> 00:04:34,565
Where's my wallet?

110
00:04:35,149 --> 00:04:37,360
There! Thank you, huh?

111
00:04:38,736 --> 00:04:41,572
Wait. Where's the 75,000?
I had 75,000 here.

112
00:04:41,656 --> 00:04:43,533
- Seventy-five?
- [Emerson] Yes!

113
00:04:43,616 --> 00:04:45,118
It's gone! They took it!

114
00:04:45,201 --> 00:04:46,035
- Gone?
- [Atoy] Seventy-five?!

115
00:04:46,119 --> 00:04:47,954
No, well… good thing.

116
00:04:48,037 --> 00:04:50,290
That wasn't really it.
This is what's most important.

117
00:04:50,373 --> 00:04:54,460
This is really what I treasure in here.

118
00:04:54,544 --> 00:04:56,004
- Mm, oh.
- [Atoy] That.

119
00:04:56,087 --> 00:04:58,798
- [Atoy] Mm. That, right? Nice.
- [Emerson mutters]

120
00:04:59,841 --> 00:05:01,301
- [Emerson] Atoy, thank you, huh?
- [Atoy] All right.

121
00:05:01,384 --> 00:05:02,802
- [Emerson] I'll go ahead.
- [Atoy] Okay, okay. Take care.

122
00:05:02,885 --> 00:05:05,638
Because, you know…
Tonet might be waiting for me.

123
00:05:05,722 --> 00:05:07,473
- [Atoy] Yes, she's waiting for you.
- Tonet's there.

124
00:05:07,557 --> 00:05:09,559
I'll go ahead. Ibyang!

125
00:05:09,642 --> 00:05:12,478
Bye, Bro Emerson!
Say hi to Sis Tonet for me.

126
00:05:12,562 --> 00:05:14,022
Okay, I'll tell her.

127
00:05:14,105 --> 00:05:15,773
- Okay, okay. Wait.
- Okay.

128
00:05:15,857 --> 00:05:16,983
Okay, bro…

129
00:05:17,692 --> 00:05:18,943
Do you have 1,500 there?

130
00:05:19,444 --> 00:05:21,654
- Please lend me 1,500.
- Why?

131
00:05:21,738 --> 00:05:25,283
- Well, I need money for fare and takeout.
- [quirky music playing]

132
00:05:25,366 --> 00:05:26,367
- [Atoy clicks tongue, mutters]
- Come on!

133
00:05:26,451 --> 00:05:28,953
- Please lend me money. I'll pay even--
- I already returned your discount,

134
00:05:29,037 --> 00:05:30,330
now you want me to give money?

135
00:05:30,413 --> 00:05:31,914
Come on. I'll pay you back.
It's just a loan.

136
00:05:31,998 --> 00:05:33,583
I'll pay you in four installments.

137
00:05:33,666 --> 00:05:35,418
- How much?
- [in English] 1,500. 1,500.

138
00:05:35,501 --> 00:05:37,628
- That, that-- Here, two… Make it two.
- Two…

139
00:05:37,712 --> 00:05:39,589
- There, that's two. Okay, fine.
- Two… That's two already.

140
00:05:39,672 --> 00:05:41,716
[in English] I love you. I love you, Atoy.
Thank you. Thank you, Atoy.

141
00:05:41,799 --> 00:05:43,009
- [mutters]
- [in English] Bye-bye!

142
00:05:43,092 --> 00:05:44,302
- Psst, hey! Get me take out, okay!
- [in English] Bye-bye!

143
00:05:44,385 --> 00:05:45,303
[Emerson] Okay, okay, okay!

144
00:05:45,386 --> 00:05:47,055
[Emerson] I got you. I love you, Atoy!

145
00:05:47,555 --> 00:05:49,640
Okay. Let's go.

146
00:05:49,724 --> 00:05:51,225
[Atoy] Ibyang.

147
00:05:51,309 --> 00:05:53,603
Let's see if we can still catch the movie.

148
00:05:53,686 --> 00:05:55,813
[music concludes]

149
00:05:55,897 --> 00:05:57,482
- [dramatic sting]
- [Tonet gasping]

150
00:05:57,565 --> 00:05:58,608
[Tonet sobs] Sis--

151
00:05:58,691 --> 00:06:01,611
- [dramatic sting]
- [Tonet gasping]

152
00:06:04,697 --> 00:06:06,407
[in English] This is all your fault.

153
00:06:07,408 --> 00:06:09,285
You know too much.

154
00:06:09,368 --> 00:06:11,579
[in English] So, it's just--

155
00:06:11,662 --> 00:06:13,998
[in English] It's… It's better
if you die. I mean…

156
00:06:14,082 --> 00:06:16,417
[in English] I-I wish I could say
I'm sorry, but I'm not!

157
00:06:17,585 --> 00:06:18,920
I don't want to die.

158
00:06:19,003 --> 00:06:21,172
[Martina shushing]

159
00:06:21,255 --> 00:06:22,715
[in English] Just-- Just--

160
00:06:22,799 --> 00:06:24,717
- Help… Help.
- [Martina, in English] Shut up!

161
00:06:24,801 --> 00:06:26,469
[Martina sighs]

162
00:06:26,552 --> 00:06:27,470
Help.

163
00:06:27,553 --> 00:06:29,722
[Martina panting]

164
00:06:29,806 --> 00:06:31,265
[coughing]

165
00:06:31,349 --> 00:06:33,643
[Martina gasping]

166
00:06:33,726 --> 00:06:38,731
- [tense music playing]
- [Tonet whimpering]

167
00:06:41,734 --> 00:06:42,985
‪-[music intensifies]
‪-[gasping]

168
00:07:01,337 --> 00:07:02,338
[Red] Hey!

169
00:07:02,839 --> 00:07:04,173
- Where did you come from?
- [Martina sighs]

170
00:07:04,257 --> 00:07:06,342
I couldn't find Tonet.
Looks like she evaded us.

171
00:07:07,301 --> 00:07:08,344
It's fine.

172
00:07:09,011 --> 00:07:10,304
[in English] She's gone.

173
00:07:11,013 --> 00:07:12,265
Oh--

174
00:07:12,348 --> 00:07:13,683
Dead?

175
00:07:14,267 --> 00:07:16,185
She was still gasping for air earlier,
but I think she's dead.

176
00:07:16,269 --> 00:07:18,646
[in English] Can you… Can you make sure?

177
00:07:19,647 --> 00:07:21,232
Where? Where's the body?

178
00:07:21,315 --> 00:07:23,526
There, at the vacant retail space.

179
00:07:23,609 --> 00:07:24,819
At the corner.

180
00:07:24,902 --> 00:07:26,446
She was hit by falling scaffolding.

181
00:07:26,529 --> 00:07:28,531
[suspicious music playing]

182
00:07:28,614 --> 00:07:29,449
[sighs] All right.

183
00:07:29,532 --> 00:07:31,951
I'll find a way to dispose of the body,

184
00:07:32,577 --> 00:07:34,120
so no one sees it.

185
00:07:34,704 --> 00:07:35,872
Did anyone see you?

186
00:07:35,955 --> 00:07:37,707
I don't think so. [gasps]

187
00:07:37,790 --> 00:07:39,876
[music swells]

188
00:07:41,294 --> 00:07:42,503
[Red] Go to the car.

189
00:07:42,587 --> 00:07:43,504
Go on.

190
00:07:44,297 --> 00:07:45,882
I still need to fix something.

191
00:07:45,965 --> 00:07:47,592
- We'll call each other, okay?
- [in English] Go.

192
00:07:59,020 --> 00:08:03,649
Has the woman arrived yet?
The one waiting for me, my sister?

193
00:08:03,733 --> 00:08:05,359
No one has arrived yet, sir.

194
00:08:05,443 --> 00:08:07,153
[suspicious music playing]

195
00:08:07,236 --> 00:08:10,448
Netchai is taking so long.
I got here late.

196
00:08:11,365 --> 00:08:13,868
I'll sit here first.
Is this the reservation under Emerson?

197
00:08:13,951 --> 00:08:15,745
- Yes, sir. Here.
- Okay, fine.

198
00:08:16,245 --> 00:08:18,080
- I'll just wait.
- Here's the menu.

199
00:08:18,164 --> 00:08:19,749
Okay, thanks.

200
00:08:20,249 --> 00:08:21,292
[in English] Thank you.

201
00:08:21,918 --> 00:08:24,086
Okay, okay…

202
00:08:24,170 --> 00:08:25,296
I have a voucher.

203
00:08:25,379 --> 00:08:28,341
[music swells]

204
00:08:29,634 --> 00:08:31,636
So, where do you want to eat?

205
00:08:31,719 --> 00:08:33,221
[music fades]

206
00:08:33,304 --> 00:08:35,765
Let's go to The Lechon House!

207
00:08:35,848 --> 00:08:37,558
Let's meet up with Sis Tonet!

208
00:08:37,642 --> 00:08:38,768
Lechon House?

209
00:08:38,851 --> 00:08:40,645
Ew. Lechon?

210
00:08:41,354 --> 00:08:44,899
I want burger and fries.
Not lechon. Gross!

211
00:08:44,982 --> 00:08:48,611
No, let's not.
Emerson is on a date with his sister.

212
00:08:48,694 --> 00:08:52,782
[muffled chattering in the distance]

213
00:08:58,120 --> 00:09:04,043
[ominous music playing]

214
00:09:06,754 --> 00:09:07,880
This is Tonet's, right?

215
00:09:08,464 --> 00:09:09,882
[Ibyang] Yes.

216
00:09:11,300 --> 00:09:12,718
[Janine] Sis Tonet?

217
00:09:13,302 --> 00:09:14,262
Uh--

218
00:09:14,929 --> 00:09:15,930
[mutters] Where could…

219
00:09:32,196 --> 00:09:33,030
‪[dramatic sting]

220
00:09:36,325 --> 00:09:37,535
‪[dramatic sting]

221
00:09:37,618 --> 00:09:38,786
Ibyang, get the bag.

222
00:09:45,334 --> 00:09:47,211
Damn, Atoy. He beat me to it.

223
00:09:47,295 --> 00:09:48,421
‪[dramatic sting]

224
00:09:48,504 --> 00:09:50,673
[music fades]

225
00:09:56,721 --> 00:10:01,183
[suspicious music playing]

226
00:10:17,742 --> 00:10:20,453
Let's get out of here. It looks dangerous.

227
00:10:22,997 --> 00:10:23,956
Come on.

228
00:10:26,959 --> 00:10:27,793
‪[dramatic stinging]

229
00:10:29,587 --> 00:10:30,921
Tatoy…

230
00:10:31,631 --> 00:10:33,341
Something's moving…

231
00:10:34,091 --> 00:10:35,718
- [tense music playing]
- [soft grunt]

232
00:10:35,801 --> 00:10:37,386
Maybe it's a kitten!

233
00:10:40,348 --> 00:10:41,766
It's moving.

234
00:10:42,767 --> 00:10:44,477
Maybe-- Move aside, move aside.

235
00:10:45,853 --> 00:10:49,148
[music swells]

236
00:10:49,982 --> 00:10:50,941
‪[dramatic sting]

237
00:10:53,402 --> 00:10:54,820
Sister Tonet?

238
00:10:57,031 --> 00:10:58,157
Tonet?

239
00:10:58,240 --> 00:11:01,494
[intense music playing]

240
00:11:01,577 --> 00:11:03,454
[music fades]

241
00:11:04,038 --> 00:11:08,626
[suspicious music playing]

242
00:11:15,049 --> 00:11:16,133
[line rings]

243
00:11:16,217 --> 00:11:18,469
[phone ringing]

244
00:11:19,470 --> 00:11:20,679
Martina.

245
00:11:21,972 --> 00:11:24,350
Hon, have you seen Tonet?

246
00:11:25,476 --> 00:11:27,395
Atoy got ahead of me.

247
00:11:28,062 --> 00:11:29,814
I think he already saw the body.

248
00:11:29,897 --> 00:11:30,940
I'm just waiting for him to come out.

249
00:11:31,023 --> 00:11:32,775
[Martina, in English] <i>Oh my God, Red!</i>

250
00:11:32,858 --> 00:11:34,860
[in English] <i>Anyway, I need you</i>
<i>to do something.</i>

251
00:11:34,944 --> 00:11:38,489
<i>This is important so we won't</i>
<i>be implicated in what happened to Tonet.</i>

252
00:11:38,572 --> 00:11:40,825
- What is it?
- [in English] <i>I need a distraction.</i>

253
00:11:41,534 --> 00:11:43,160
[in English] <i>Pull out the fire alarm.</i>

254
00:11:47,081 --> 00:11:48,207
[music fades]

255
00:11:48,290 --> 00:11:49,417
Tonet?

256
00:11:49,500 --> 00:11:54,088
[pensive music playing]

257
00:11:54,964 --> 00:11:56,590
- [Tonet mutters]
- [Atoy] Tonet.

258
00:11:57,675 --> 00:11:58,968
What happened to you?

259
00:11:59,552 --> 00:12:02,179
I have to say-- I have to say--

260
00:12:02,263 --> 00:12:03,848
Tonet, don't talk anymore. I'll get help.

261
00:12:03,931 --> 00:12:05,558
[coughs]

262
00:12:05,641 --> 00:12:07,893
- Sir, your order, sir.
- [in English] Thank you.

263
00:12:21,949 --> 00:12:23,409
What's the matter with you, Netchai?

264
00:12:24,743 --> 00:12:27,288
[alarm blaring]

265
00:12:29,665 --> 00:12:33,043
Ma'am, sir, we need to leave.
The fire alarm is sounding.

266
00:12:33,127 --> 00:12:35,880
Ma'am and sir, we need to evacuate.
The fire alarm is sounding.

267
00:12:35,963 --> 00:12:37,548
- This way.
- [patron] Oh no, I brought something--

268
00:12:37,631 --> 00:12:40,134
- [indistinct]
- [line rings]

269
00:12:40,217 --> 00:12:42,261
Netchai, I can't reach you.

270
00:12:42,344 --> 00:12:44,722
Sir, we need to evacuate.

271
00:12:44,805 --> 00:12:46,098
The fire alarm is sounding.

272
00:12:46,849 --> 00:12:49,477
- But what about my order?
- [waiter] We'll pack it.

273
00:12:49,560 --> 00:12:51,270
All right, all right.
Please pack it quickly.

274
00:12:51,353 --> 00:12:52,855
I'll get the bill, and here's the voucher.

275
00:12:53,439 --> 00:12:55,399
- The voucher.
- Yes, sir.

276
00:12:55,483 --> 00:12:56,817
- I'll get the bill.
- Yes, sir.

277
00:12:56,901 --> 00:12:57,943
All right.

278
00:12:58,027 --> 00:13:02,198
[alarm blaring]

279
00:13:02,281 --> 00:13:03,991
[tense music playing]

280
00:13:04,074 --> 00:13:07,870
- [clatters]
- Ah, unbelievable!

281
00:13:09,163 --> 00:13:10,289
Oh no!

282
00:13:10,372 --> 00:13:11,499
[alarm blaring]

283
00:13:11,582 --> 00:13:12,917
[hiss] What's that?

284
00:13:14,502 --> 00:13:16,253
[clicks tongue]

285
00:13:16,337 --> 00:13:18,714
[alarm blaring]

286
00:13:18,797 --> 00:13:22,134
[ominous music playing]

287
00:13:24,136 --> 00:13:25,638
Ibyang, Janine, get out! Hurry!

288
00:13:25,721 --> 00:13:27,348
[alarm blaring]

289
00:13:27,431 --> 00:13:28,474
[Atoy] Get out now!

290
00:13:29,225 --> 00:13:30,976
[sobs] Tatoy…

291
00:13:31,060 --> 00:13:32,811
I'll stay with Sister Tonet.

292
00:13:32,895 --> 00:13:34,647
Please get help.

293
00:13:34,730 --> 00:13:35,856
[alarm blaring]

294
00:13:35,940 --> 00:13:37,691
[Atoy] Stay with her. Stay with her.

295
00:13:37,775 --> 00:13:38,859
[alarm blaring]

296
00:13:38,943 --> 00:13:41,195
Sir, here's your order, sir.

297
00:13:41,278 --> 00:13:43,113
[alarm blaring]

298
00:13:43,197 --> 00:13:44,365
[in English] Okay, okay.

299
00:13:44,448 --> 00:13:45,741
All right, thanks.

300
00:13:46,242 --> 00:13:48,285
Ah, thank you.

301
00:13:48,369 --> 00:13:52,164
[muttering]

302
00:13:55,918 --> 00:13:58,420
Sister Tonet, don't close your eyes.

303
00:13:58,504 --> 00:14:00,339
Don't close your eyes.

304
00:14:00,422 --> 00:14:02,424
- [sobbing]
- [Tonet gasps]

305
00:14:02,508 --> 00:14:04,635
Sister… don't close your eyes.

306
00:14:04,718 --> 00:14:07,596
You still have lunch with Brother Emerson.

307
00:14:08,681 --> 00:14:09,848
Lechon! [sobbing]

308
00:14:09,932 --> 00:14:12,851
Janine-- Janine…

309
00:14:12,935 --> 00:14:17,231
Janine… Janine… She's not…

310
00:14:17,314 --> 00:14:20,276
She's not… She's not…

311
00:14:21,318 --> 00:14:23,195
She's not…

312
00:14:23,279 --> 00:14:24,864
[music fades]

313
00:14:24,947 --> 00:14:27,449
[Ibyang] Sister Tonet! Sis Tonet!

314
00:14:27,533 --> 00:14:29,159
Sister Tonet, wake up!

315
00:14:29,243 --> 00:14:31,912
Sister Tonet, wake… wake up!

316
00:14:31,996 --> 00:14:34,373
I love you so much, Sister Tonet!

317
00:14:34,456 --> 00:14:37,001
Please, please! Wake up!

318
00:14:37,084 --> 00:14:38,335
[Ibyang wailing]

319
00:14:38,419 --> 00:14:41,338
Wake up!

320
00:14:41,422 --> 00:14:43,215
Please!

321
00:14:43,299 --> 00:14:44,967
Sister Tonet!

322
00:14:45,050 --> 00:14:47,428
Sister Tonet!

323
00:14:47,511 --> 00:14:49,638
I love you so much!

324
00:14:49,722 --> 00:14:52,558
[dramatic music playing]

325
00:14:53,726 --> 00:14:57,688
[muffled chattering]

326
00:14:59,148 --> 00:15:00,816
Where's Netchai?

327
00:15:01,984 --> 00:15:03,569
Where did you--

328
00:15:03,652 --> 00:15:04,862
[woman 1] Why is there a fire alarm?

329
00:15:04,945 --> 00:15:06,155
There doesn't seem to be a fire.

330
00:15:06,238 --> 00:15:08,073
They said someone had
an accident, probably dead.

331
00:15:08,657 --> 00:15:10,117
- Dead?
- Yes.

332
00:15:10,200 --> 00:15:11,243
What-- What happened?

333
00:15:11,327 --> 00:15:13,037
Someone had an accident?

334
00:15:13,537 --> 00:15:14,955
Yes, maybe dead.

335
00:15:15,039 --> 00:15:20,085
[indistinct chattering]

336
00:15:21,670 --> 00:15:25,299
[pensive music playing]

337
00:15:36,435 --> 00:15:37,436
Atoy!

338
00:15:38,479 --> 00:15:39,438
Atoy!

339
00:15:39,521 --> 00:15:41,857
[indistinct chattering]

340
00:15:45,736 --> 00:15:47,529
[ambulance siren wailing]

341
00:15:47,613 --> 00:15:48,614
Atoy!

342
00:15:49,740 --> 00:15:50,616
Atoy!

343
00:15:51,784 --> 00:15:53,994
I'll take you home first
before I go to the hospital.

344
00:15:54,078 --> 00:15:55,037
I'll have your mom pick you up.

345
00:15:55,120 --> 00:15:56,330
[in English] Okay, Daddy.

346
00:15:56,413 --> 00:15:59,583
No one wanted this to happen.
Pray for your Aunt Tonet, okay?

347
00:16:00,084 --> 00:16:01,043
Come on.

348
00:16:01,126 --> 00:16:02,836
- [Atoy] Let's go, let's go.
- [Emerson] Atoy?

349
00:16:04,046 --> 00:16:06,340
Oh? You took so long to come out.

350
00:16:06,840 --> 00:16:08,175
Is it true there's a fire?

351
00:16:08,884 --> 00:16:10,177
Fire?

352
00:16:10,260 --> 00:16:12,888
It's um… It's Tonet. [clicks tongue]

353
00:16:12,972 --> 00:16:15,599
She didn't show up at the restaurant.
Did you see her?

354
00:16:15,683 --> 00:16:17,267
I can't contact her.

355
00:16:18,143 --> 00:16:19,645
Maybe she went home.

356
00:16:21,939 --> 00:16:24,400
Who was put in the ambulance?

357
00:16:24,483 --> 00:16:25,776
And why were you there?

358
00:16:27,903 --> 00:16:28,779
Bro…

359
00:16:31,490 --> 00:16:32,992
Bro, Tonet had an accident.

360
00:16:33,075 --> 00:16:36,453
[tense music playing]

361
00:16:37,246 --> 00:16:39,415
She's the one we put in the ambulance.

362
00:16:39,498 --> 00:16:42,876
[dramatic sting]

363
00:16:43,544 --> 00:16:45,587
We just saw her with the kids.

364
00:16:46,213 --> 00:16:48,465
She was impaled--

365
00:16:48,549 --> 00:16:50,342
[gasps]

366
00:16:50,426 --> 00:16:51,719
Sorry, bro.

367
00:16:51,802 --> 00:16:53,929
[dramatic sting]

368
00:16:54,013 --> 00:16:55,180
[titters]

369
00:16:55,264 --> 00:16:57,725
[melancholic music playing]

370
00:16:57,808 --> 00:16:59,018
- [Atoy] Sorry, bro.
- [scoffs]

371
00:16:59,101 --> 00:16:59,935
- [Atoy] Bro.
- [scoffs]

372
00:17:05,524 --> 00:17:09,445
[ambulance siren wailing]

373
00:17:12,781 --> 00:17:13,657
[Emerson] Netchai!

374
00:17:14,158 --> 00:17:16,326
[music fades]

375
00:17:16,952 --> 00:17:19,705
[suspicious music playing]

376
00:17:19,788 --> 00:17:23,500
They already took Tonet's body,
but I have no update on her status.

377
00:17:24,752 --> 00:17:27,337
[in English] Well, I hope
she's really dead.

378
00:17:27,421 --> 00:17:29,673
Because if she's still alive,
then we're dead.

379
00:17:32,342 --> 00:17:33,719
What was the fire alarm for?

380
00:17:35,929 --> 00:17:37,431
[alarm blaring]

381
00:17:39,641 --> 00:17:40,726
‪[dramatic stinging]

382
00:17:51,737 --> 00:17:54,364
[Martina, in English] <i>We kept on</i>
<i>chasing her around the mall!</i>

383
00:17:54,448 --> 00:17:56,867
<i>If somebody sees us,</i>
<i>for sure, we'll be suspects!</i>

384
00:17:57,701 --> 00:17:58,786
[Red] <i>Good thing you thought of that.</i>

385
00:17:58,869 --> 00:18:00,996
[alarm blaring]

386
00:18:01,080 --> 00:18:05,042
[tense music playing]

387
00:18:05,125 --> 00:18:06,168
[music fades]

388
00:18:06,251 --> 00:18:09,088
[ambulance siren wailing]

389
00:18:09,171 --> 00:18:10,089
[Emerson panting] Stop!

390
00:18:10,172 --> 00:18:11,423
Stop!

391
00:18:11,507 --> 00:18:12,508
[panting]

392
00:18:12,591 --> 00:18:15,094
Stop that! My sister is in there!

393
00:18:15,177 --> 00:18:17,346
Stop, stop! Let me in!

394
00:18:17,429 --> 00:18:19,098
Open this! Open this!

395
00:18:19,181 --> 00:18:22,226
My sister is in there!
Sis! Open this! Sis!

396
00:18:22,309 --> 00:18:23,644
Sis! Open this!

397
00:18:23,727 --> 00:18:24,978
[panting]

398
00:18:25,062 --> 00:18:26,271
Netchai?

399
00:18:26,980 --> 00:18:27,981
Netchai?

400
00:18:28,857 --> 00:18:31,235
What-- What happened?

401
00:18:31,318 --> 00:18:32,653
What happened?

402
00:18:32,736 --> 00:18:34,613
Netchai. Netchai.

403
00:18:34,696 --> 00:18:36,323
- [melancholic music playing]
- [panting]

404
00:18:36,406 --> 00:18:39,451
[heavy breathing, gasps]

405
00:18:39,535 --> 00:18:42,704
Netchai, what happened?

406
00:18:42,788 --> 00:18:45,874
[Emerson sniffles, sobs]

407
00:18:45,958 --> 00:18:49,753
Netchai? Netchai! Netchai.

408
00:18:50,254 --> 00:18:53,924
[stammers] Brother is here.
Netchai, Brother is here now.

409
00:18:54,007 --> 00:18:54,842
[smooches]

410
00:18:54,925 --> 00:18:55,926
[Emerson] I'm here.

411
00:18:56,009 --> 00:18:58,637
Hmm, I'm sorry. I didn't--

412
00:18:58,720 --> 00:19:00,639
I didn't get here right away.

413
00:19:00,722 --> 00:19:02,516
Here's the lechon.

414
00:19:02,599 --> 00:19:04,518
Here's our lechon.

415
00:19:04,601 --> 00:19:06,854
You wanted this, right? [sobs]

416
00:19:06,937 --> 00:19:09,106
Netchai. [sobbing]

417
00:19:09,189 --> 00:19:14,361
Don't give up, Netchai. [sobs]

418
00:19:14,444 --> 00:19:17,156
Don't give up, okay?

419
00:19:17,239 --> 00:19:19,199
Brother is here.

420
00:19:19,283 --> 00:19:20,701
[sobbing]

421
00:19:20,784 --> 00:19:27,207
[in Visayan] Didn't I promise you
that I will look after you?

422
00:19:27,791 --> 00:19:28,876
Netchai…

423
00:19:28,959 --> 00:19:31,837
[sobbing]

424
00:19:31,920 --> 00:19:36,884
[Emerson singing]
♪ <i>Little one, little one, sleep now…</i> ♪

425
00:19:36,967 --> 00:19:37,801
[sobs]

426
00:19:37,885 --> 00:19:43,307
♪ <i>Your mother isn't here…</i> ♪

427
00:19:45,017 --> 00:19:46,351
[Emerson in Visayan]
<i>Didn't we make a promise?</i>

428
00:19:47,269 --> 00:19:48,478
[in English] Promise?

429
00:19:48,562 --> 00:19:49,980
[in Visayan] No one will leave.

430
00:19:50,063 --> 00:19:54,193
- [in English] Promise?
- [in English] Promise. Promise.

431
00:19:54,276 --> 00:19:56,153
[gentle music playing]

432
00:19:56,236 --> 00:19:58,780
[humming gentle tune]

433
00:19:58,864 --> 00:20:01,158
[Emerson sobbing] ♪ <i>Your mother</i> ♪

434
00:20:01,241 --> 00:20:05,245
♪ <i>Little one, little one…</i> ♪

435
00:20:05,329 --> 00:20:09,374
[humming and sobbing]

436
00:20:09,458 --> 00:20:15,172
- [dramatic music playing]
- [sobbing]

437
00:20:15,255 --> 00:20:19,885
[sobbing]

438
00:20:34,775 --> 00:20:37,736
[Cita] My God, Atoy!
How did Tonet end up there?

439
00:20:37,819 --> 00:20:40,781
What would she be doing
in a vacant mall space?

440
00:20:41,281 --> 00:20:42,658
I don't know.

441
00:20:42,741 --> 00:20:46,411
The police and the mall manager
will come here to talk to us.

442
00:20:46,912 --> 00:20:49,873
Brother, Sis Tonet's wounds
aren't that bad, right?

443
00:20:49,957 --> 00:20:51,750
She'll be able to overcome this, right?

444
00:20:52,542 --> 00:20:53,460
[Cita] My God.

445
00:20:54,294 --> 00:20:55,837
[doctor clears throat]

446
00:20:56,713 --> 00:20:58,674
- [pensive music playing]
- [door clicks shut]

447
00:20:58,757 --> 00:21:01,301
Doctor. Doctor, what's the news?

448
00:21:01,885 --> 00:21:03,762
Uh, are you the relative of the patient?

449
00:21:03,845 --> 00:21:05,722
Where's her sibling?

450
00:21:07,849 --> 00:21:09,184
[music swells]

451
00:21:09,268 --> 00:21:10,185
Uh--

452
00:21:11,353 --> 00:21:13,605
[music fades]

453
00:21:14,606 --> 00:21:15,565
[in English] Lord…

454
00:21:17,109 --> 00:21:18,235
[sniffles]

455
00:21:19,194 --> 00:21:20,654
I'm sorry if…

456
00:21:24,825 --> 00:21:26,785
it took me a while to…

457
00:21:27,369 --> 00:21:29,454
speak to You sincerely.

458
00:21:30,289 --> 00:21:32,582
It took me a while to reach out to You.

459
00:21:36,503 --> 00:21:38,380
Please don't be upset with me.

460
00:21:38,463 --> 00:21:42,592
[gentle music playing]

461
00:21:42,676 --> 00:21:44,720
But this is an emergency.

462
00:21:49,683 --> 00:21:51,226
Please save…

463
00:21:51,310 --> 00:21:52,561
[sobs]

464
00:21:52,644 --> 00:21:54,104
…my sister.

465
00:21:55,772 --> 00:21:57,566
Have mercy on her.

466
00:22:00,610 --> 00:22:02,779
She's still young, and…

467
00:22:04,239 --> 00:22:06,992
she still has so much she can do in life.

468
00:22:23,425 --> 00:22:24,634
Lord, please…

469
00:22:27,846 --> 00:22:29,473
give this to her.

470
00:22:34,227 --> 00:22:35,145
If…

471
00:22:35,979 --> 00:22:39,775
If You want, take some from me
and give it to her instead.

472
00:22:48,366 --> 00:22:49,242
[Tonet] Brother.

473
00:22:50,869 --> 00:22:53,663
[music fades]

474
00:22:53,747 --> 00:22:56,792
[sentimental music playing]

475
00:22:56,875 --> 00:22:58,168
- Netchai.
- [Tonet chuckles]

476
00:22:58,251 --> 00:23:01,254
Oh? How did you get out of the OR?

477
00:23:01,338 --> 00:23:02,380
Are you okay now?

478
00:23:03,048 --> 00:23:04,966
Don't worry about me.

479
00:23:05,926 --> 00:23:08,011
I'm more worried about you.

480
00:23:08,929 --> 00:23:11,223
You should take care of yourself.

481
00:23:13,642 --> 00:23:15,852
Don't be too hot-headed.

482
00:23:15,936 --> 00:23:19,606
And cut down on all that lechon.

483
00:23:20,190 --> 00:23:25,987
And your foot, have it checked
because you keep stumbling.

484
00:23:26,613 --> 00:23:28,490
[chuckles]

485
00:23:28,573 --> 00:23:31,993
And be kind to the people you meet.

486
00:23:33,995 --> 00:23:36,498
Open your heart to them.

487
00:23:40,043 --> 00:23:41,837
What are you saying?

488
00:23:42,629 --> 00:23:43,839
What are you saying?

489
00:23:43,922 --> 00:23:46,550
[gentle music playing]

490
00:23:46,633 --> 00:23:49,719
Don't let yourself be sad for too long,

491
00:23:49,803 --> 00:23:51,847
because that's a waste of time.

492
00:23:53,223 --> 00:23:55,058
The world is waiting for you.

493
00:23:58,687 --> 00:24:01,773
And I just want you to know…

494
00:24:02,440 --> 00:24:05,110
you're my favorite person,

495
00:24:05,193 --> 00:24:07,445
and I'm so proud of you.

496
00:24:07,529 --> 00:24:09,781
[both chuckling]

497
00:24:10,365 --> 00:24:11,825
I love you so much.

498
00:24:12,617 --> 00:24:13,910
[both chuckling]

499
00:24:14,494 --> 00:24:15,745
Here-- [scoffs]

500
00:24:16,246 --> 00:24:17,581
Oh, c'mon.

501
00:24:17,664 --> 00:24:19,916
What's the matter with you, Netchai?
You're so OA.

502
00:24:20,000 --> 00:24:21,793
You're being so dramatic!

503
00:24:22,294 --> 00:24:24,588
What's wrong with you? Wait. Sit here.

504
00:24:24,671 --> 00:24:26,923
Tell me. What happened?

505
00:24:27,007 --> 00:24:29,259
What really happened? Come, sit here.

506
00:24:29,342 --> 00:24:31,553
Later, later I'll tell you.

507
00:24:31,636 --> 00:24:33,346
But for now, look!

508
00:24:33,430 --> 00:24:35,557
Miss Cita is there. Go to her first.

509
00:24:35,640 --> 00:24:37,809
Yes, I'll just stay here. I'll sit here.

510
00:24:38,393 --> 00:24:39,519
Promise, I'll stay here.

511
00:24:41,980 --> 00:24:42,981
[Tonet] I'll stay here.

512
00:24:47,319 --> 00:24:48,570
Wait a moment, okay. Wait.

513
00:24:48,653 --> 00:24:53,366
[melancholic music playing]

514
00:25:03,126 --> 00:25:04,961
Miss Cita, is there a problem?

515
00:25:05,462 --> 00:25:06,421
Emerson…

516
00:25:09,090 --> 00:25:12,761
Uh, Tonet's operation is finished.

517
00:25:13,637 --> 00:25:15,931
Uh, we spoke with the doctor.

518
00:25:16,431 --> 00:25:18,225
[sobs]

519
00:25:18,308 --> 00:25:19,643
[gentle music playing]

520
00:25:19,726 --> 00:25:20,852
- [sobs]
- [Emerson] Miss Cita.

521
00:25:21,436 --> 00:25:25,232
[sobbing]

522
00:25:25,315 --> 00:25:28,068
[Cita, in English]
I'm sorry, Emerson. [sobs]

523
00:25:28,151 --> 00:25:30,528
Tonet didn't make it.

524
00:25:30,612 --> 00:25:34,115
She lost too much blood.

525
00:25:34,199 --> 00:25:36,534
[sobs] Emerson, she's gone.

526
00:25:36,618 --> 00:25:39,120
[sobbing]

527
00:25:39,204 --> 00:25:40,121
Miss Cita…

528
00:25:40,205 --> 00:25:41,581
- [sobs]
- [titters]

529
00:25:41,665 --> 00:25:43,959
- What are you saying, Miss Cita?
- Emerson…

530
00:25:44,042 --> 00:25:46,670
Miss Cita, come on.
I just spoke with Tonet, right there!

531
00:25:46,753 --> 00:25:48,964
[sobs] Emerson…

532
00:25:49,047 --> 00:25:53,468
Her body has already
been moved to the morgue.

533
00:25:54,052 --> 00:25:55,095
[sobs]

534
00:25:55,178 --> 00:25:56,137
Netchai?

535
00:25:56,221 --> 00:25:57,472
[sobs]

536
00:25:57,555 --> 00:25:58,598
Netchai?

537
00:25:59,140 --> 00:26:01,017
[sobbing]

538
00:26:01,101 --> 00:26:02,352
No, no!

539
00:26:02,435 --> 00:26:04,145
Miss Cita, what you're saying
is impossible.

540
00:26:04,229 --> 00:26:07,607
I just spoke with Tonet.
She even told me to go to you.

541
00:26:07,691 --> 00:26:10,568
She's right here. Netchai! Netchai?

542
00:26:10,652 --> 00:26:13,446
Miss Cita, don't prank me!

543
00:26:13,530 --> 00:26:15,699
I was talking to my sister.
She's right here!

544
00:26:15,782 --> 00:26:18,493
My sister is right here! Netchai!

545
00:26:18,576 --> 00:26:20,245
[Cita] She's gone, Emerson.

546
00:26:20,328 --> 00:26:21,621
- Emerson--
- No.

547
00:26:21,705 --> 00:26:23,290
No, Miss Cita. What are you--

548
00:26:23,373 --> 00:26:25,041
Ah, Miss Cita, don't prank me--

549
00:26:25,125 --> 00:26:27,085
[Cita] Tonet just made you
feel her presence.

550
00:26:27,168 --> 00:26:28,295
No!

551
00:26:28,378 --> 00:26:30,839
- To assure you she's okay--
- Miss Cita, no, no--

552
00:26:30,922 --> 00:26:32,424
[shouting] Miss Cita, she can't be dead!

553
00:26:32,507 --> 00:26:34,676
She can't be dead, Miss Cita!

554
00:26:34,759 --> 00:26:36,177
My sister can't be dead!

555
00:26:36,261 --> 00:26:38,138
I was just hugging her here!

556
00:26:38,221 --> 00:26:40,390
I was hugging my sister here!

557
00:26:40,473 --> 00:26:42,600
Netchai was here just now!

558
00:26:42,684 --> 00:26:43,852
She was here!

559
00:26:43,935 --> 00:26:46,021
- [Cita] She's gone!
- Netchai! Netchai!

560
00:26:46,104 --> 00:26:48,440
- No, Emerson, she's gone!
- Where's my sister--

561
00:26:48,523 --> 00:26:50,400
No! [bawls]

562
00:26:50,483 --> 00:26:52,861
- Emerson, Tonet is gone!
- No!

563
00:26:53,361 --> 00:26:55,989
No! My sister! [bawls]

564
00:26:56,698 --> 00:26:58,950
- My sister!
- [Cita] Emerson…

565
00:26:59,534 --> 00:27:02,287
- Emerson…
- Where's my sister-- No!

566
00:27:02,370 --> 00:27:04,414
She can't be dead!

567
00:27:04,497 --> 00:27:06,958
She can't be dead, Miss Cita!

568
00:27:07,042 --> 00:27:08,960
- She's gone.
- I was just with my sister!

569
00:27:09,044 --> 00:27:11,963
- Emerson. She's gone.
- She was just here now.

570
00:27:12,505 --> 00:27:14,090
[sobbing] She was just here.

571
00:27:14,174 --> 00:27:16,426
[sobbing continues]

572
00:27:16,509 --> 00:27:17,427
She was here--

573
00:27:17,510 --> 00:27:20,555
[sobs] She's gone-- She's gone.

574
00:27:20,638 --> 00:27:23,224
[melancholic music playing]

575
00:27:23,308 --> 00:27:26,644
- She's left us.
- [sobbing and wailing]

576
00:27:26,728 --> 00:27:28,646
Emerson, Tonet is gone.

577
00:27:28,730 --> 00:27:30,648
- She's left us.
- [wailing and sobbing]

578
00:27:33,943 --> 00:27:35,445
Emerson…

579
00:27:35,945 --> 00:27:39,449
- [sobbing and wailing]
- [music fades]

580
00:27:39,532 --> 00:27:42,660
[electronic blipping]

581
00:27:42,744 --> 00:27:47,290
[tense music playing]

582
00:27:49,876 --> 00:27:52,921
According to witnesses,

583
00:27:53,004 --> 00:27:56,257
there was a man
forcing her to go with him,

584
00:27:56,341 --> 00:27:58,009
saying she stole from him.

585
00:27:58,093 --> 00:28:01,012
Who was that man accusing her

586
00:28:01,096 --> 00:28:02,013
- of stealing?
- [inaudible]

587
00:28:02,097 --> 00:28:02,889
- Hey.
- Ah--

588
00:28:02,972 --> 00:28:04,307
Why did you bump into me? Are you blind?

589
00:28:04,391 --> 00:28:05,517
I know you.

590
00:28:05,600 --> 00:28:07,102
[Cita] <i>Red Regalia?</i>

591
00:28:07,185 --> 00:28:10,438
I suspect Tonet's death
wasn't an accident.

592
00:28:10,522 --> 00:28:12,399
So, now you'll be a policeman?

593
00:28:12,482 --> 00:28:14,984
[Mercado] <i>You'll need an ID and a badge.</i>

594
00:28:15,068 --> 00:28:16,528
<i>I can't produce that.</i>

595
00:28:16,611 --> 00:28:18,279
[Red] <i>Maybe you should go</i>
<i>to the wake tomorrow.</i>

596
00:28:18,363 --> 00:28:21,616
Find out what's on their mind.
Find out what's on Atoy's mind.

597
00:28:21,699 --> 00:28:23,660
[Red] <i>He's a tracker. So, he's like a spy.</i>

598
00:28:23,743 --> 00:28:26,663
<i>He probably has another theory</i>
<i>about Tonet's death.</i>

599
00:28:27,205 --> 00:28:28,790
Our condolences.

600
00:28:28,873 --> 00:28:30,375
[in English] My condolences.

601
00:28:30,458 --> 00:28:31,501
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

602
00:28:31,584 --> 00:28:33,128
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

603
00:28:33,211 --> 00:28:35,213
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

604
00:28:35,296 --> 00:28:38,174
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

605
00:28:38,883 --> 00:28:40,427
♪ <i>Fix it</i> ♪

606
00:28:40,510 --> 00:28:41,803
Subtitle translation by: Rachel C. Arias
